.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH AMIVULN 1  amivuln 
.SH NAME
amivuln \- Am I vulnerable? Backport\-aware CVE check for packages on this host
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBamivuln\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-epss\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-distro\fR] [\fB\-\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-purl\fR] [\fB\-\-baseline\fR] [\fB\-\-vex\fR] [\fB\-\-packages\-from\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fITARGET\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports which CVEs apply to an installed package, binary or version, taking the patches your distribution already shipped into account. Fedora and Arch Linux are supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format: summary, detail, json, sarif, markdown, csv or prometheus
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the result to FILE instead of stdout, replacing it atomically
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Exit 1 when a finding reaches this level: none, low, medium, high, critical or kev
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-epss\fR \fI<SCORE>\fR
Exit 1 when an affected finding has at least this EPSS score (0.0 to 1.0)
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Count findings without a distro statement as violations of \-\-fail\-on
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Never use the network; answer from the cache only
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
Do not keep a cache on disk for this run
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Configuration file (skips the default search path)
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colors: auto, always or never (`NO_COLOR` is honored)
.TP
\fB\-\-distro\fR \fI<DISTRO>\fR
Treat the host as another distro: `fedora:44` or `arch`
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Treat this path as a target (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<NAME[@VERSION]>\fR
Treat this value as an installed package name or `name@version` (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-purl\fR \fI<PURL>\fR
Treat this value as a package URL (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
A previous `\-f json` report; only new findings violate \-\-fail\-on
.TP
\fB\-\-vex\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
`OpenVEX` documents stating that a product is not affected (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\-from\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Check the packages listed in FILE (one `name@version` per line) instead of the installed ones; for example a list exported from another host
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Only print errors
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Check every installed package
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fITARGET\fR]
Targets to check: package name, file path, `name@version` or purl
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
amivuln\-check(1)
Check packages, files, versions or purls
.TP
amivuln\-cve(1)
Is this host affected by a CVE? Scans every installed package
.TP
amivuln\-pending(1)
Which updates close the most risk? Ranks the updates that fix affected findings
.TP
amivuln\-services(1)
Check every running systemd service. Services that are not packaged are listed, not fatal
.TP
amivuln\-restart(1)
Which running processes still use files an update replaced? Exit 1 when a restart is needed
.TP
amivuln\-mcp(1)
Serve read\-only tools to AI agents over the Model Context Protocol on stdio
.TP
amivuln\-config(1)
Show, create or validate the configuration
.TP
amivuln\-cache(1)
Inspect or clear the on\-disk cache
.TP
amivuln\-completions(1)
Print shell completions
.TP
amivuln\-version(1)
Print version and build information
.TP
amivuln\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Finished; no finding at or above \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR.
.TP
1
Finished; findings at or above \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR.
.TP
2
The result is incomplete: a required source was unavailable and no usable cached copy existed. Never treat this as a clean result.
.TP
3
A target could not be resolved (not found, ambiguous, or no detectable version).
.TP
64
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
70
Internal error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check an installed package:
.PP
.RS
amivuln nginx
.RE
.PP
Check the package that owns a file:
.PP
.RS
amivuln /usr/sbin/nginx
.RE
.PP
Check every installed package and fail a build on HIGH or worse:
.PP
.RS
amivuln \-\-all \-\-fail\-on high
.RE
.PP
Check a version for another distribution, for example in a CI container:
.PP
.RS
amivuln openssl@3.5.1\-1 \-\-distro arch \-f json
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI./.amivuln.toml\fR, \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/amivuln/config.toml\fR, \fI/etc/amivuln/config.toml\fR
Configuration, first one found wins. See \fBamivuln config init\fR.
.TP
\fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/amivuln/cache.sqlite\fR
HTTP cache.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBAMIVULN_FORMAT\fR, \fBAMIVULN_FAIL_ON\fR, \fBAMIVULN_OFFLINE\fR, \fBAMIVULN_CONFIG\fR, \fBAMIVULN_COLOR\fR
Same as the corresponding options.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Disables colors when set to a non\-empty value.
.SH PRIVACY
Only the ecosystem, the package name and the version leave the host. There is no telemetry.
